# Tailwind Usage - Essential Rules

## ✅ ALWAYS Use Tailwind Classes Inline

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT - Pure Tailwind with design system colors
<div className="flex items-center gap-4 p-6 bg-background text-foreground rounded-lg">
<Link className="px-4 py-2 hover:bg-card transition-colors">
<header className="w-full bg-background text-foreground" style={{ borderBottom: "1px solid var(--border)" }}>
```

## ❌ NEVER Create Custom CSS Classes

```css
/* ❌ FORBIDDEN - Don't create custom classes */
.app-header {
  background-color: var(--background);
}
.nav-link:hover {
  background-color: var(--card);
}
.custom-button {
  padding: 1rem;
}
```

## 🎯 Borders Exception (Tailwind v4 Issue)

```tsx
// ❌ WRONG - Tailwind border classes don't work
<div className="border border-border">

// ❌ WRONG - Common violation pattern
<div className="bg-card border border-border rounded-lg">

// ✅ CORRECT - Use inline styles for borders
<div style={{ border: "1px solid var(--border)" }}>
<div style={{ border: "2px dashed var(--border)" }}>
<div className="bg-card rounded-lg" style={{ border: "1px solid var(--border)" }}>
```

## ✅ Only 2 Valid Custom CSS Cases

1. **Theme-based logo switching** (can't be done with Tailwind)
2. **Complex `@keyframes` animations**

Everything else? **Pure Tailwind inline classes.**

## 🎯 Key Rules

- **Maximize Tailwind**: Use `hover:`, `focus:`, `bg-*`, `text-*` inline
- **No Custom CSS**: Don't create `.custom-class` for styling
- **Design System Colors**: Use `bg-background`, `text-foreground`
- **Borders Exception**: Use `style={{ border: "..." }}` only
- **NEVER use `border border-border`** - This is a common violation!
- **Self-Documenting**: All styling visible in component
